1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,320
 Want to know the secret to getting your toddler to stop hitting?

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,940
 It's not threatening them.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,480
 It's not shaming them.

4
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,940
 It's not coming in hot with a no.

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,680
 We do not do that.

6
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:15,260
 Because when you blow up, when you lose your cool, when you come in hot with a big no,

7
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,260
 two things happen.

8
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:22,500
 One, for a toddler, a big reaction can actually feel exciting and fun and it gives them that

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,680
 attention that they so desperately crave from us, which means we can accidentally reinforce

10
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:29,720
 that behavior to happen more.

11
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:36,200
 Two, it can make your already emotionally volatile kid more volatile in the moment.

12
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,360
 When you go the other direction and you do nothing, your kid learns that hitting is totally

13
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,360
 okay.

14
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:45,960
 So how do you stop the hitting?

15
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:50,620
 Come in calm, confident, I know that part's hard, and okay the feelings.

16
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:51,820
 It's okay to feel mad.

17
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:54,800
 The feeling that your child's feeling in the moment is okay.

18
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,160
 The behavior is not.

19
00:00:57,160 --> 00:01:01,320
 So next you come in with a boundary and I'm talking words and action.

20
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,220
 Together, it sounds like this.

21
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,280
 It's okay to feel mad.

22
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,720
 It is not okay to hit.

23
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,920
 I'm picking up baby to keep him safe.

24
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:11,820
 And then later, once they're calm, which is when the brain can take in new information

25
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:16,880
 and learn new skills, go back and talk about what they were feeling and what they can do

26
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:22,320
 next time when they feel that way or they're in that situation instead of hitting.

27
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,920
 We're not always going to get it right.

28
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:28,760
 The goal is progress, not perfection, but this is how we're going to raise resilient

29
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:29,420
 generation.

